      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don't think this is necessary. When sorted by Activity, Age Gated instances will always show on top, no matter how many users are in the instance. Even when sorted by Friends, Age Gated instances will show up below instances in which you have friends.\n\nThe reason you probably don't see those instances is because they reached a threshold. For example, in Murder 4, once an instance reaches more than 13 users, the instance disappears from the listing, but can still be joined if you are part of the group (it still shows if a friend is present in the instance).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-10-23T05:19:28.568Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Under instances, there's sort by active and friends. I noticed that there isn't a filter for age restrictioned instances. This would be convenient to add, as I have to reopen the menu several times before one shows up frequently.",
